  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 153 PM CDT Fri Aug 21 2026\n\nSaturday night through Friday\nAssessment...low (20-30%) confidence on rain around Wednesday\n\nNorthwest flow aloft will persist through the coming week. The best \nchance for any rain looks to be tied to around Wednesday during the \npassage of yet another cool front. However, this system will only \nhave the moisture associated with it. As a result, the model \nconsensus only has 20-30% chances for rain.\n\nPrior to and after next Wednesday, there will be additional but \nweaker upper level disturbances moving through in the flow aloft. \nWhile an isolated shower or storm cannot be ruled out, over 90% of \nthe area will likely remain dry with near seasonable temperatures.",
